# OpenAxis — Frontend Rules

## Component Structure
- Wrap ALL Node views in `<NodeWrapper>` — provides security and theme framing
- Keep components focused — split into smaller components when a file exceeds ~200 lines

## Styling
- Tailwind utilities ONLY — no custom CSS files
- Dark mode palette:
  - Background: `gray-950` / Surface: `gray-900` / Borders: `gray-800`
  - Text: `gray-100` primary, `gray-400` secondary, `gray-500` muted
  - Accent: `orange-500` (internal), `blue-500` (external), `green-500` (safe), `red-500` (danger)
- Cards: `rounded-lg border border-gray-800`

## Responsive Design
- Mobile-first: default styles are mobile, use `md:` and `lg:` for larger screens
- Feed views: single-column (max-w-xl centered), stacked on mobile

## Data Fetching
- Use TanStack Query for ALL API calls — no bare `fetch()` in components
- Use Zustand store for cross-Node shared state (e.g., `currentFocus` ticker)

## State
```typescript
// Cross-Node shared state — set in SigWire, read in Trader
interface AxisState {
  currentFocus: string | null;  // e.g. "NVDA"
  user: User | null;
}
```

## Node Registry
- Register new Nodes in `registry.ts` with `id`, `name`, `apiUrl`, and `component`
- Use dynamic imports for Node components (lazy loading)

## Security
- Never expose API keys in frontend code — all secrets via env vars (VITE_ prefix)
- Sanitize user-generated content before rendering (avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`)
